# Emerald Rozalia — Project 1
#
# DO NOT REMOVE ANY LINE IN THIS FILE.
#
# Prettier's HTML parser does not understand Django template syntax. When it
# reformats a template it rewrites the inside of {% %} and {{ }} blocks, and
# that silently destroys the page:
#
#   1. It wraps long lines inside a tag. Django's lexer matches {%.*?%} WITHOUT
#      re.DOTALL, so a tag containing a newline stops being a tag and becomes
#      literal text. Its closing partner is then orphaned:
#
#        {% block title %}...{% endblock %}{%
#        block content %}
#        -> TemplateSyntaxError: Invalid block tag ... 'endblock'
#
#   2. It treats the tag interior as an HTML attribute list and rewrites
#      comparisons:
#
#        {% if request.GET.department == d %}
#        -> {% if request.GET.department="" ="d" %}
#
# This already happened to this project. It broke 30 of 39 templates and took
# 34 of 94 routes and 91 of 95 pages to HTTP 500. Full analysis and the repair
# plan are in TECHNICAL_ASSESSMENT.md section 2.2.
#
# If you need to format a template, use a Django-aware tool
# (e.g. djlint / djhtml), never Prettier.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

